      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Eliminating Hidden Surcharges &amp; Demanding Written Binding Contracts for Bike Transport from Hyderabad</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When you hire a packer and mover, the basic freight rate is usually based on distance, vehicle size, and weight. Dishonest transporters, however, often inflate the bill on the day of the move by adding hidden surcharges for floor elevation, long carries, or toll taxes that were never disclosed in the initial estimate.</p>

<p>Floor elevation surcharges are levied when the loading or unloading site is on a higher floor without an elevator. Long‑carry fees appear when the customer must walk a long distance between the vehicle and the house.</p>
<p>Toll‑tax surcharges are added when the transport vehicle has to cross toll booths en route. In many cases, these costs are bundled into the final invoice and are not itemised or pre‑approved, leaving the customer to pay extra on the spot.</p>

